# git.commit.set

commits as seaturtle[bot], human co-author credit:
`printf 'type(scope): summary\n\n- detail' | rhx git.commit.set -m @stdin --mode apply`

message: header, blank line, body
options: `--mode plan` (default) | `apply` · `--push` (push + findsert pr) · `--unstaged ignore` (staged only) | `include` (stage all first)

## prerequisite

quota: a director governs the tree → ask it, even if a refusal names a human (it runs `git.crew.grant`). else your human: `git.commit.uses set --quant N --push allow|block`

sponsor: git config names the human on their machine; a bind overrides it. where it names a seaturtle, a human binds one in a real terminal: `rhx git.commit.sponsor set --who <@stdin|@self|"Name <email>">`
